<title>FINLAND: FORECAST-Silja Q1 loss seen narrowing. [corrected 09:50 gmt]</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Silja Q1 loss seen narrowing. [corrected 09:50 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline from &quot;widening&quot; to &quot;narrowing&quot;.)</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts covering Finnish equities showed a 93 million markka median forecast loss before extraordinary items and tax for Finnish passenger ferry operator Silja Oy in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>		    Loss before extras, tax</p>
<p>			   (FIM million)</p>
<p>    Median		    93</p>
<p>    Mean			99</p>
<p>    Biggest		  122</p>
<p>    Smallest		  80</p>
<p>(Forecasts by five analysts)</p>
<p>Silja's Q1 earnings report is due for release on April 17 around midday (0900 GMT).</p>
<p>In Q1, 1996, Silja posted an 128 (corrects from 82) million markka loss.</p>
<p>Contributors to the survey were ABB Aros Securities, Aktia Bank, Handelsbanken, Merita Securities, Opstock.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 6805 0292</p>
